# Go Connector SDK Conventions

- Prefer precise domain names and thin public APIs.
- Use pointers for optional fields when zero has a separate meaning.
- Use apply methods for functional options, never marker interfaces plus a type
  switch.
- Seal schema-erasure interfaces with unexported methods.
- Document every hand-written public type, field, constant, interface, method,
  function, constructor, default, side effect, error, and lifecycle constraint.
  Generated declarations are exempt.
- Keep complete Go examples for related API families in package docs, READMEs,
  or runnable examples.
- Keep public signatures compatible with released tags unless the change follows
  the repository's breaking-release policy.
